eactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3448196925","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112021#issuecomment-3448196925","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112021","id":3448196925,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Nh089","user":{"login":"SkanerSoft","id":13809475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODA5NDc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13809475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft","html_url":"https://github.com/SkanerSoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SkanerSoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-26T08:31:26Z","updated_at":"2025-10-26T08:31:26Z","body":"> [@akien-mga](https://github.com/akien-mga) , am I right in understanding that you compile the Windows binaries using Linux as the host system - in other words, you use cross-compilation using not the latest compilers? Perhaps it would be better if Windows users compiled the editor and templates themselves. In that case, Windows users could build them using either the latest MinGW GCC 15.2.0 or MSVC.\n\nIt sounds like an offtop, but in fact, now users of any OS can build Godot independently for their OS.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3448196925/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3448222300","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112021#issuecomment-3448222300","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112021","id":3448222300,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Nh7Jc","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-26T08:51:17Z","updated_at":"2025-10-26T08:51:17Z","body":"Yes, there are full instructions for compiling from source in the docs, which any user can do (in theory at least):\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/3.6/development/compiling/index.html\n\nHowever the real trick is to compiling builds that will work for the widest variety of end user systems as possible, which is what the official releases strive for, using e.g. build containers with old versions of the OS etc.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3448222300/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3448391787","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112021#issuecomment-3448391787","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112021","id":3448391787,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Nikhr","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-26T10:37:05Z","updated_at":"2025-10-26T10:37:05Z","body":"Compiling your own versions with latest MSVC should work fine. Using MinGW-GCC on Windows or on Linux is the same, the difficulty here is a combination of using MinGW-GCC and LTO, which yields the best performance, but sometimes uncovers some bugs in the compiler as this combination isn't as thoroughly tested (I assume) by GCC developers than native Linux builds. Making builds with MinGW-GCC without LTO (enabled by default with `production=yes`, can be turned off with `lto=none`) should be safer but leads to losing some performance.\n\nIt's not the first time we have such issues and usually these are bugs in GCC or binutils, I'll look into it.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3448391787/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3448418706","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112021#issuecomment-3448418706","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112021","id":3448418706,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NirGS","user":{"login":"RoyalXXX","id":125651292,"node_id":"U_kgDOB31JXA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125651292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyalXXX","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyalXXX","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyalXXX/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyalXXX/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyalXXX/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyalXXX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyalXXX/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyalXXX/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyalXXX/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyalXXX/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyalXXX/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-26T10:58:04Z","updated_at":"2025-10-26T11:04:00Z","body":"> Compiling your own versions with latest MSVC should work fine. Using MinGW-GCC on Windows or on Linux is the same, the difficulty here is a combination of using MinGW-GCC and LTO, which yields the best performance, but sometimes uncovers some bugs in the compiler as this combination isn't as thoroughly tested (I assume) by GCC developers than native Linux builds. Making builds with MinGW-GCC without LTO (enabled by default with `production=yes`, can be turned off with `lto=none`) should be safer but leads to losing some performance.\n> \n> It's not the first time we have such issues and usually these are bugs in GCC or binutils, I'll look into it.\n\nI compile templates myself, since with custom compilation - even if you don’t disable individual features - the template size, and consequently the game size, is **significantly smaller**. In my experience, **MSVC performs better on Windows** compared to MinGW-GCC, both in terms of compilation and linking speed, as well as the size of the resulting binaries. Regarding performance, I haven’t noticed any difference.\n\nAdditionally, when compiling templates, it’s possible to use encryption, which doesn’t work with the official templates. Of course, encryption isn’t a form of DRM, since the key is stored in the binary, but it does provide some protection against script kiddies.\n\nAs for compiling the editor, I’ve never had the need to build it myself, as the official binaries have always worked perfectly. This is just an exceptional case.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3448418706/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3452029423","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112021#issuecomment-3452029423","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112021","id":3452029423,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Nwcnv","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-27T15:51:03Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T15:51:03Z","body":"Thanks everyone for the reports and testing.\n\nClosing as solved in the rebuilt 3.6.2-stable, and the underlying buildsystem issue is tracked in https://github.com/godotengine/build-containers/issues/157.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3452029423/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]